Let the line be $(a x+2 b y+3 b)+\lambda(b x-2 a y-3 a)=0\because$ It is parallel to $x$-axis.
$\therefore \frac{\mathrm{a}+\mathrm{b} \lambda}{2 \mathrm{a} \lambda-2 \mathrm{ b}}=0 \Rightarrow \lambda=-\frac{\mathrm{a}}{\mathrm{ b}}$ So, equation is $a x+2 b y+3 b-\frac{a}{b}(b x-2 a y-3 a)=0\begin{aligned}
& \Rightarrow a x+2 b y+3 b-a x+\frac{2 a^2 y}{b}+\frac{3 a^2}{b}=0 \Rightarrow\left(2 b+\frac{2 a^2}{b}\right) y=-\left(\frac{3 a^2}{b}+3 b\right) \\
& \Rightarrow y=-\frac{3}{2}
\end{aligned}$

